- Story & Context: Dockside myth across the illegal coastal yards of Cobh insists that thousands of blind abyssal organisms have begun synchronizing their seasonal mating swarms to the transatlantic data pulses leaking from cracked underwater cables. Diver-turned-producer Joshua Flynn documented the phenomenon during his final deep-water descent into the Romanche Trench, watching millions of bioluminescent silt-moths spiral in chaotic polyrhythmic clouds around the humming fiber line while his violin hydrophone picked up a brutal 158 BPM kick pattern rattling through the seabed. When Flynn returned to the surface with bloodshot eyes and fractured hearing, he looped the seabed vibrations into an explosive ten-minute anthem, muttering through the final vocal take: "Leave di surface, break di skin, let di trench-hatch crawl within."
